{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january","id":1156946,"title":"kickstarter in January","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-08T03:27:56-08:00","id":1156946,"title":"kickstarter in January","content":"So the Monday Meeting notes said that the kickstarter will be in January 2018, what do people hope for in terms of stretch goals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T05:00:37-08:00","id":1156967,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that the KS is gonna be for the Continuum corebook and Aeon, which means stuff for Aeon, the present day, and setting-neutral stuff is all potentially on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T07:51:16-08:00","id":1157006,"title":"","content":"The stretch goals will probably be close to the Scion ones. Factions other than the Psi Orders, Political groups, dice (at a much lower tier this time, I hope!) Pregenerated characters, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T07:52:55-08:00","id":1157008,"title":"","content":"maybe/hopefully a jumpstart, those are useful for those new to the system + setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T08:18:04-08:00","id":1157015,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends on what we get from the core. I wouldn't be opposed to alternate modes, or maybe a small supplement on cool advanced tech. In general I like it when the offer the stretch goal that give the contractors a small pay bump. Just seems real classy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T08:42:23-08:00","id":1157021,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting one, because Aeon and core Continuum are distinct genres - Aeon is future sci-fi kitchen sink, while core Continuum is present-day action-adventure kitchen sink.<br /> <br /> So, what might be likely?<br /> <br /> T-shirts. That's basically an OP given at this point.<br /> Jumpstarts for both settings.<br /> Pregens for both settings.<br /> Extra Allegiances for both.<br /> Aeon translation guide.<br /> ...An anthology would be odd. I could see limiting it to Aeon or the core, or opening up the breadth of the Continuum.<br /> Something like the Demon Seed collection for Demon: the Descent - book(s) of locations where interesting stuff's going down. Would be particularly nice for Aeon, showcasing the range of sci-fi subgenres it has.<br /> LARP rules, perhaps? They did it for Scion...<br /> Something from Earplay.<br /> Possibly era books where you'd only need Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T09:04:01-08:00","id":1157026,"title":"","content":"Something that was done for WtA, and MtAs was a m20/w20 cookbook, and thats just great, it is something i can only see working for Aeon, giving us food from across the different orders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T11:27:52-08:00","id":1157071,"title":"","content":"Keep them coming, folks! Loving all your ideas and it's great to get them ahead of time to parse into our own list. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T12:34:18-08:00","id":1157094,"title":"","content":"it seems like a big ask, but, something i loved from Exalted second edition was the comics, i mean rather than intro fiction it had intro comics, now i'm not going to suggest these comics in the core book, but having some of the the fiction in say an anthology for Aeon being done as comics would be really cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T13:01:11-08:00","id":1157103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1157094#post1157094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems like a big ask, but, something i loved from Exalted second edition was the comics, i mean rather than intro fiction it had intro comics, now i'm not going to suggest these comics in the core book, but having some of the the fiction in say an anthology for Aeon being done as comics would be really cool</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. Maybe something like the Exalted 3E KS, which managed to get a comic as a stretch goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T13:10:33-08:00","id":1157105,"title":"","content":"yeah something like that, i mean trinity is so pulpy, hell aberrant is superhero based, surely these are generas where comics belong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T17:53:41-08:00","id":1157159,"title":"","content":"I think I'd be into an era book or two. A tech book would be great too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T01:23:50-08:00","id":1157219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B][URL=&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">marin[/URL]&quot;[/B]]This is an interesting one, because Aeon and core Continuum are distinct genres - Aeon is future sci-fi kitchen sink, while core Continuum is present-day action-adventure kitchen sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what?!? I thought that &quot;continuum&quot; meant the whole spread from Adventure to Trinity, the universe these exist in as it were. What's this about being a separate genre, or present day?? I'm so confused. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20880-murdoc","name":"Murdoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20880_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T03:03:16-08:00","id":1157231,"title":"","content":"the core continuum book is going to contain a modern day action adventure setting, presumably so you can play something with just that book, rather than needing both continuum core + aeon or aberrant (whenever that comes out) or whatever other setting book you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T07:23:20-08:00","id":1157273,"title":"","content":"Any interest in music for the settings? I know they have done it before, and I think we could get some really interesting pieces out of Aeon. one of the problems I see is going to needing to offer things that can fit in with both the modern and the scifi settings simultaneously. So that you don't have a tier stall because only part of the fan base wants to throw money at it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T16:23:37-08:00","id":1157655,"title":"","content":"Thanks <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather\">ahather</a>,</b> although I don't know why. What made these games great was their settings, so now they put in some other generic setting as well, and then give it a confusing name? I don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20880-murdoc","name":"Murdoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20880_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:42:27-08:00","id":1157680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murdoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1157655#post1157655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">ahather</a>,</b> although I don't know why. What made these games great was their settings, so now they put in some other generic setting as well, and then give it a confusing name? I don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you find confusing? Aeon, Aberrant, and Adventure! were always the same setting, and now we're looking at more cool parts of that setting. Since we have the chance to look at pretty much any time, or even alternative times/dimensions, we're calling that overall setting the Trinity Continuum. Rather than just put out a core system rule book, we're also making that book a viable part of the Continuum by having the modern day setting in it. Hope that helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:58:54-08:00","id":1157786,"title":"","content":"In my head, I keep renaming the modern day setting &quot;ACTION&quot; in keeping with the &quot;A&quot; pattern, and forgetting that isn't actually the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T16:56:09-08:00","id":1157835,"title":"","content":"Thank you <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\">RichT</a></b> for your reply, but I'm afraid that I am still failing to understand. Maybe it's because I am a long time Trinity/Aberrant player but new to these forums, and thus unfamiliar with certain things about Onyx Path's vision that are sometimes taken for granted; I don't know. So if you will indulge me a bit further, I'll try to explain my problem more precisely. My confusion is two-fold:<br /> 1) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we have the chance to look at pretty much any time, or even alternative times/dimensions, we're calling that overall setting the Trinity Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been my understanding. &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot; == Trinty+Aberrant+Adventure; that entire universe and timeline. However, now I am being told that &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot; == specific time period related to &quot;modern&quot; real life for some kind of action/adventure setting. It's a sub-setting, like &quot;Trinity&quot; OR &quot;Aberrant&quot; OR &quot;Adventure.&quot; So which is it? Or is the term being used for both somehow, which would be the explanation for my confusion?<br /> 2) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and now we're looking at more cool parts of that setting... by having the modern day setting in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, in the previous Trinity universe setting, the &quot;modern day&quot; bit was Aberrant. However from what I have been gleaning from the forums Aberrant is going to be moved to a later time. This, along with the idea of having a fourth time period that is not Adventure, Aberrant, or Trinity, would put it in between Adventure and Aberrant. Previously there was nothing really interesting happening in the between time periods, at least from the perspective of playing a game of super-humans with powers. So my question is why? I understand what you said about your reason to want to make a core book independent of the three main sub-settings/time periods, as well as to make that book playable by including its own. So I just want to know what is it that is interesting about this sub-setting, as in, why might I want to play it? (honest question tone, not a criticism one) For all I know now it is just like modern day with nothing special, except perhaps with the Aeon Society doing little things in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20880-murdoc","name":"Murdoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20880_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T16:59:11-08:00","id":1157836,"title":"","content":"I would love a section with the typical archetypes of the era or character examples to streamline the process of character creation. <br /> A supplement about gadgets and mad science is a must. I've never got the feeling that I could play one in the previous books.<br /> Another supplement about how to create the batcave. Well, okay not just the batcave, you know what I mean. A book about how to create cool hero headquarters and evil lairs.<br /> A book about the organizations and most importantly, how they interact with each other and the world at large. Give us a story and a system to make them feel alive. <br /> That's it for now, I will post more if I can think about something else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T18:35:40-08:00","id":1157844,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20880-murdoc\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar20880_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20880\" data-vbnamecard=\"20880\">Murdoc</a> No offense taken. Let me see if I can cover most of your concerns/questions. Generally, the first go around of our three lines wasn't a master plan to only do those three, those are just the ones we did (and Adventure! I had to fight to publish). We are using The Trinity Continuum as the umbrella name for all of the setting, from ancient times, through the three you are familiar with, to the far future. Aberrant was a &quot;a few years from the present&quot; timeframe, and since we are now a fair bit past that present with this edition, we've pushed it forward again. The Trinity Continuum Core, the right now in the present book, is designed to allow Jason Bourne, John Wick the movies, Leverage and Ocean's Eleven, style play. Basically, characters that aren't super-heroes, but which are capable of heroic actions. The universe of the Trinity Continuum rewards those who try, who strive to change reality, if you will, and so our characters can be totally normal folks, or extremely good (and lucky) at what they do. As for whether there is anything interesting going on, that'll be our goal to draw you into each of these new eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T20:12:02-08:00","id":1157861,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\">RichT</a></b> Thanks I think that does clear things up. Although I think that you probably should have a name for that era/sub-setting perhaps, it might help. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Trinity Continuum Core, the right now in the present book, is designed to allow Jason Bourne, John Wick the movies, Leverage and Ocean's Eleven, style play.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you hadn't used the John Wick example (which I've never heard of), I'd think that you must know me or something, because I love those other 3 enough you've practically got me sold on the idea right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd so <u><i>love</i></u> to play a game like that! (In fact in the Aberrant game I ran for years I put in an NPC named David Webb who worked for the Directive, using Jason Bourne's real name to throw the players off of who I was stealing him from. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20880-murdoc","name":"Murdoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20880_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T03:26:43-08:00","id":1157901,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> are more science orientated characters playable in the Action setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","user":"ahather","date":".  fixing errors 11-12-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T05:35:16-08:00","id":1157910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1157901#post1157901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> are more science orientated characters playable in the Action setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of 'uber-dev' Ian Watson is that the Continuum core will have a Super-Science section, including rules for Advanced Science (mundane tech about a decade ahead of its time), Inspired Science (tech which can only be created by one of the Inspired, but usable by anyone), and Powered Science (tech that can only be created and used by the Inspired, as it's powered by their Source, most likely Psi or Quantum).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T08:44:34-08:00","id":1157942,"title":"","content":"There are also two rival Allegiances focused on superscience and technology in the modern setting, as well as room for scientific characters in other groups. (And there might be a different era called ACTION! later...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:28:45-08:00","id":1158017,"title":"","content":"I agree with the others. The Trinity Continuum Corebook Setting needs some kind of name of its own (other than 'Trinity Core setting', which is a mouthful, and also basically wrong).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T23:54:05-08:00","id":1158098,"title":"","content":"Hm. They might be noodling this around already, but would people be up for licensed community content, a la <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Vault</a>, as a stretch goal? (For those unfamiliar with it, this would mean you could put fan stuff for the Continuum up for sale on a royalty basis, as long as you adhered to Onyx Path's guidelines.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":".  Clarifying I'm suggesting this as a stretch goal 11-13-2017, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T08:16:32-08:00","id":1158172,"title":"","content":"Thinking more about this. This would only be an Aeon stretch, but maybe a small supplement that details the intra and extra solar colonies? There was some detail on this in first edition, but I was always surprised there wasn't more detailed info about Mars and the other intra-solar holdings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T13:31:50-08:00","id":1159153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1157942#post1157942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also two rival Allegiances focused on superscience and technology in the modern setting, as well as room for scientific characters in other groups. (And there might be a different era called ACTION! later...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda like Action! to be the title of the contemporary setting. Totally sets the tone. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T18:55:31-08:00","id":1159295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murdoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1157835#post1157835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) This has always been my understanding. &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot; == Trinty+Aberrant+Adventure; that entire universe and timeline. However, now I am being told that &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot; == specific time period related to &quot;modern&quot; real life for some kind of action/adventure setting. It's a sub-setting, like &quot;Trinity&quot; OR &quot;Aberrant&quot; OR &quot;Adventure.&quot; So which is it? Or is the term being used for both somehow, which would be the explanation for my confusion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Continuum encompasses the entire timeline (which includes Aeon, Aberrant and Adventure!). The Trinity Continuum core rulebook also contains a modern-day era, so people have a straightforward game about modern day heroism right out of the rulebook before they start looking into other time periods and Inspired types. The modern day is sort of a default setting and doesn't have its own name. I'd like to remind people of that: it's not called &quot;Action,&quot; which is a name we may be using later for another era, and if we do I'd like to avoid confusion now rather than later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, in the previous Trinity universe setting, the &quot;modern day&quot; bit was Aberrant. </div> </div> </div>Aberrant was released in 1999, and was set in 2008, with supplements taking it up to 2015. So it was set 10-15 years in the future, rather than <i>today</i> (whenever &quot;today&quot; is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However from what I have been gleaning from the forums Aberrant is going to be moved to a later time. </div> </div> </div>Since we're 20 years later from the original game, Aberrant's getting pushed forward 20 years to 2028. It's still &quot;near future,&quot; by about the same amount as the original game was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This, along with the idea of having a fourth time period that is not Adventure, Aberrant, or Trinity, would put it in between Adventure and Aberrant. Previously there was nothing really interesting happening in the between time periods, at least from the perspective of playing a game of super-humans with powers. </div> </div> </div>As the original tagline for Adventure! said, <i>Every age has its heroes</i>. There may not be any superhumans, but that doesn't mean there isn't anything interesting going on. That's why Talents -- what Adventure! called daredevils -- are available right from the core.<br /> <br /> Besides which, even the original games had sprinkled suggestions of strange events in the past which weren't otherwise covered by a published era. For example, the timeline portion of the original Aeon said there was a surge of people with powers in 1970, and we never heard anything else about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So my question is why? I understand what you said about your reason to want to make a core book independent of the three main sub-settings/time periods, as well as to make that book playable by including its own. So I just want to know what is it that is interesting about this sub-setting, as in, why might I want to play it? (honest question tone, not a criticism one) For all I know now it is just like modern day with nothing special, except perhaps with the Aeon Society doing little things in the background. </div> </div> </div>I recommend you take a look at some of the Allegiance previews we've posted. Some of the material has since changed, but it should give you an idea of the setting (as well as some interesting connections between Adventure! and Aberrant if you're astute).<ul><li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-9-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">9</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-les-fantomes-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Les Fantomes</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-theseus-club-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">The Theseus Club</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-transcendent-alliance-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">The Transcendent Alliance</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-neptune-foundation-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">The Neptune Foundation</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-archangel-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Archangel</a></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T17:04:54-08:00","id":1160367,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\">IanWatson</a></b>, I understand things much better now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrant was released in 1999, and was set in 2008, with supplements taking it up to 2015. So it was set 10-15 years in the future, rather than <i>today</i> (whenever &quot;today&quot; is). Since we're 20 years later from the original game, Aberrant's getting pushed forward 20 years to 2028. It's still &quot;near future,&quot; by about the same amount as the original game was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it. I understand that the default time to start play was 2008 before, but what I meant by &quot;modern&quot; was that the events of Aberrant started in 1999, with the Fireman and all that, so that was pretty much the same time as IRL. So is it going to be the same/similar in the new version? If the default game start is 2028, is the original incidents going to be 9 years or so before, in 2019? Not exactly today, but pretty close. And if so, how will that affect the default nameless subsetting set today (-ish, whenever the game comes out)? Will that be part of the things to do is watch the Aberrant era kick off (once you have that supplement anyway)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20880-murdoc","name":"Murdoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20880_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T22:34:50-08:00","id":1160428,"title":"","content":"Sorry for apparently setting off the \u201cAction\u201d confusion with my comment about what I keep calling it in my head. I didn\u2019t mean to confuse anyone into thinking it was the real name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T22:38:22-08:00","id":1160430,"title":"","content":"I do really like the balance of Adventure! being set in the 1920s, Aberrant in the 2020s, and Aeon in the 2120s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T13:02:08-08:00","id":1162242,"title":"","content":"So, what would I like for strech goals. Actually, nothing. I want it all in the first place! ;-) But since you asked:<br /> <br /> - Arts! I like great arts in RPGs. Would be a shame to read through a dozen pages in the books without being distracted by a pic which lets you dive into the setting and getting an additional idea for your next session<br /> <br /> - I'm big fan of the Aeon Trinity game. I don't know how exactly the setting has changed (orders, politics etc.). If in a high enough degree, an additional book about orders, colonies, aliens, technology, general life etc. would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T08:20:56-08:00","id":1162464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1162242#post1162242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm big fan of the Aeon Trinity game. I don't know how exactly the setting has changed (orders, politics etc.). If in a high enough degree, an additional book about orders, colonies, aliens, technology, general life etc. would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see stretch goals focussed on expanding the setting material greatly: space exploration, exploring extrasolar colonies, alien worlds, alien races, the various solar system habitats and nations (instead of them being tied necessarily to order splat books) - preferably leaving out anything about deep-space 'novas', keep it Psion/2120 specific. Gimme more Aeon era setting fluff and quite I'm happy. No interested in things like fiction. No interest in 1st edition PDF libraries and anything else not original for the tweaked setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T08:28:13-08:00","id":1162465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1162464#post1162464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to see stretch goals focussed on expanding the setting material greatly: space exploration, exploring extrasolar colonies, alien worlds, alien races, the various solar system habitats and nations (instead of them being tied necessarily to order splat books) - preferably leaving out anything about deep-space 'novas', keep it Psion/2120 specific. Gimme more Aeon era setting fluff and quite I'm happy. No interested in things like fiction. No interest in 1st edition PDF libraries and anything else not original for the tweaked setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the library'll probably be a pledge tier, going by previous KSes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T19:21:56-08:00","id":1163143,"title":"","content":"I'd be into a book of art. Maybe it's a comic, maybe not. But a large gallery of locations, people, tech, etc would be kind of awesome beyond what fits in the game books. Would for sure love for every piece of tech to have artwork or schematics. This is likely a pipe dream but an app for keeping track of your character(s) on your phone might be nice. I love the piece of paper but I'm spitballing a bit here. Dice apps are great and a branded one may be fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T10:46:22-08:00","id":1163279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1162465#post1162465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, the library'll probably be a pledge tier, going by previous KSes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly they'll be available one way or another - old edition PDFs keep coming up in other Kickstarters so there must be enough interest in that kind of offering - and/or its a really cheap way to add &quot;stuff&quot; to a KS. As someone who has them all already for Aeon, plus multiple copies of each print book it's not a consideration for me, YMMV of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T05:15:05-08:00","id":1164228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1163279#post1163279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost certainly they'll be available one way or another - old edition PDFs keep coming up in other Kickstarters so there must be enough interest in that kind of offering - and/or its a really cheap way to add &quot;stuff&quot; to a KS. As someone who has them all already for Aeon, plus multiple copies of each print book it's not a consideration for me, YMMV of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 1st edition PDFs don't interest me either as I also own them already. I also don't care for the Earplays from Pugmire. I prefer the stretch goals be something I can actually hold in my grubby hands. Perhaps a deal with a site like Hero Forge to make Trinity style miniatures? Paizo just did a KS for miniatures to go with their Starfinder line but they cost a fortune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:23:34-08:00","id":1164552,"title":"","content":"I have a question: Is the Kickstarter just for the core book is Aeon included like with Scion?<br /> <br /> Also, will there be a draft text preview similar to Cavaliers of Mars or Dark Eras 1?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:49:58-08:00","id":1164647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1164552#post1164552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question: Is the Kickstarter just for the core book is Aeon included like with Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've said it'll include both the Trinity Continuum core RPG, and the AEON rpg books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1164552#post1164552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, will there be a draft text preview similar to Cavaliers of Mars or Dark Eras 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T18:41:58-08:00","id":1164938,"title":"","content":"So looking forward to this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T22:22:45-08:00","id":1165236,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I will not be able to fund this one. After having to wait well over a year for my Scion books I no longer have faith in the capacity of onyx path to deliver a product in anything like a timely manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:34:01-08:00","id":1165948,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to have a pledge tier for having a location named in the world. Perhaps a planet for Aeon, a building or something for Aberrant, and perhaps a company or something like that? Name a something, basically. <br /> <br /> A great stretch goal would be an actual play with Ian and others playing the game. Perhaps their could be a pledge level for this too. I'd also love to see an audio play or a mini-comic at the very least as others have mentioned. <br /> <br /> This is a long shot, but I'd love a Divis Mal action figure as a stretch goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my products on the ST Vault here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/225678/Dark-New-England-Five-Chronicle-Jumpstarts-Bundle?affiliate_id=235787\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/pro...iate_id=235787</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12515-inclusivegaming","name":"InclusiveGaming","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:59:43-08:00","id":1166007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1165236#post1165236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately I will not be able to fund this one. After having to wait well over a year for my Scion books I no longer have faith in the capacity of onyx path to deliver a product in anything like a timely manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>You kidding? They're only like two months late at this point. That's not a huge delay. That's barely a blip. And they've been completely upfront about <i>why</i> they're late, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:59:45-08:00","id":1166008,"title":"","content":"Scion KS gave stretch goals of stuff like &quot;Satyrs and Amazons in the companion book.&quot; I really liked that, just entirely new things to do, make, play, or fight against...caused my group to throw in an extra 5-10 each, so we broke 100 on it. So basically...that. Stretch goals that give us more non fluff stuff. I dont need settings, unless the rules are different in that setting. I dont need or want more npc's. I dont need premade characters. I Really dont need the old books...I own every official and fan made supplement for all 3 lines(except the never completed Adventure! fan companion...grr...) in physical AND PDF copy. I want more tech, more aliens, more powers, etc. I will throw a damn bitcoin at it if i see &quot;Conversion rules for 1st edition to 2nd&quot; or &quot;Conversion for Scion to Trinity Continuum&quot;! This goes as well for future Aberrant KS and Adventure! My group of 6 are looking at almost 100 a piece for Aberrant...we really like Aberrant...ABERRANT! (Yes Man redbull joke)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T03:26:07-08:00","id":1166043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1166007#post1166007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You kidding? They're only like two months late at this point. That's not a huge delay. That's barely a blip. And they've been completely upfront about <i>why</i> they're late, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The physical books were supposed to come out two months ago, the PDFs, what I am waiting for, were supposed to come out eight months ago.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T08:45:48-08:00","id":1167005,"title":"","content":"My big hope is they keep to the general events, themes and moods of the games. Including the presence of Divis Map, one of the first gay and powerful rpg characters that I remember seeing and whixh made me feel included by the designers. <br /> <br /> What I don't want is something like how Mummy the Curse said it was a new version of Mummy the Ressurrection and them gave me something that spit on the themes of the game I loved for years. (I'm still bitter about this.) So yeah if the themes are the same then I an very much looking forward to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 12-12-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T09:50:02-08:00","id":1167020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1167005#post1167005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big hope is they keep to the general events, themes and moods of the games. Including the presence of Divis Map, one of the first gay and powerful rpg characters that I remember seeing and whixh made me feel included by the designers. <br /> <br /> What I don't want is something like how Mummy the Curse said it was a new version of Mummy the Ressurrection and them gave me something that spit on the themes of the game I loved for years. (I'm still bitter about this.) So yeah if the themes are the same then I an very much looking forward to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand how you might have been disappointed, but Mummy: The Curse was created specifically for Chronicles of Darkness (previously New World of Darkness) and was never advertised as a new version of the WoD Mummy game lines. The Trinity Continuum is specifically about being new versions of the first editions of the Trinity games, and while I can't guarantee that every single thing will be in there or be presented the same way, we're not designing these lines from scratch and all of us have long histories with the games and are aiming to include those elements that make the games what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:17:45-08:00","id":1167037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1167020#post1167020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we're not designing these lines from scratch and all of us have long histories with the games and are aiming to include those elements that make the games what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Divis Mal has arms!: confirmed. Awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:21:45-08:00","id":1167072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1167037#post1167037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Divis Mal has arms!: confirmed. Awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>....Always!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:23:40-08:00","id":1167073,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, Divis Mal's arms were in fact one of the first things confirmed after the new edition was announced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1166043#post1166043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The physical books were supposed to come out two months ago, the PDFs, what I am waiting for, were supposed to come out eight months ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, however, that the delay on Scion has largely been due to late system adjustments from incorporating refinements originally implemented by the Trinity writers. Those refinements, however, will already be in Trinity. So, fingers crossed, Trinity is unlikely to suffer a similar delay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":171,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","user":"MythicFox","date":". 12-12-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T13:08:48-08:00","id":1167101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1167020#post1167020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can understand how you might have been disappointed, but Mummy: The Curse was created specifically for Chronicles of Darkness (previously New World of Darkness) and was never advertised as a new version of the WoD Mummy game lines. <br /> <br /> The Trinity Continuum is specifically about being new versions of the first editions of the Trinity games, and while I can't guarantee that every single thing will be in there or be presented the same way, we're not designing these lines from scratch and all of us have long histories with the games and are aiming to include those elements that make the games what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this. I don't expect 100% sameness (in fact some elements should be changed) but if you keep the themes and moods and elements and even some of the cool characters, which it sounds like you will, then I'm excited. Very excited. <br /> <br /> I still have faith in you guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the other point, well, for all that I like some of the mechanics what happened to its theme has never has sat well with me (and I hate how the power stat goes 10 to 1, hate it). It's worse since I kickstarted it and didn't feel like I was made aware of the how things were going to be so radically different. Unfortunately, the Curse forms still be all about how amazing it is so I havent even bothered posting since then. <br /> <br /> But pardon me, as that's got nothing to do with Trinity so it's basically not on topic. <br /> <br /> What is is saying, thumbs up to you guys for the update to the setting. <br /> <br /> Ps. Divis Mal, and his arms, are awesome!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T13:25:26-08:00","id":1167760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1156946-kickstarter-in-january?p=1167037#post1167037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Divis Mal has arms!: confirmed. Awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, Exalted 2E confirmed that Divis has FOUR arms :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","c